1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,660
[Disclaimer: This series is created
solely for entertainment purposes.

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:03,330
All individuals, behaviors, places,
and events depicted are entirely fictional,

3
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:05,000
with no intention to represent or reference any
organizations, departments, occupations, or individuals]

4
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:08,240
I don't want you to be
in this terrible relationship.

5
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:11,000
You make the person you're with feel seen

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,740
and acknowledged.

7
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:13,700
That's the reason

8
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:15,720
I want to be your friend.

9
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,620
If you still hold each other back,

10
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:19,360
no one is going to be happy.

11
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:25,000
We were never friends, Chris...

12
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:30,080
What's most important about food is taste.

13
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:33,560
But taste is made up of texture,

14
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:34,920
smell,

15
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:36,720
experience,

16
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:38,880
and memory.

17
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:09,320
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

18
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:14,440
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

19
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:18,340
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

20
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:24,560
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

21
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:34,300
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

22
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:39,360
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

23
00:01:39,380 --> 00:01:43,660
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

24
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:52,320
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

25
00:01:52,840 --> 00:02:01,480
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

26
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:19,280
Chris,

27
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:22,000
cooking with flowers

28
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:23,460
isn't easy.

29
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:25,940
That means it's possible?

30
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:36,660
Doing something and
being good at it are two different things.

31
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:38,240
But I think

32
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:39,380
this is good.

33
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:02,280
I'm buying it,

34
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:04,380
both you...

35
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:07,720
and your food.

36
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:18,840
It's so good.

37
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:21,060
Really?

38
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:22,200
Well done.

39
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,640
You got it on your face.

40
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:52,480
Let's give it a try.

41
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,920
The terms remain the same.

42
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,480
You'll work behind the scenes,

43
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:00,720
and you can start the PR plan right away.

44
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:02,280
Mm.

45
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:04,080
Since she's already done this much...

46
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:06,600
Why not at least let her train the chefs?

47
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:08,480
As for the restaurant,

48
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:10,280
I'll take care of Chris.

49
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:12,840
If customers have questions,

50
00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:15,360
she can answer them about her inspiration.

51
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:16,760
I'll take care of her.

52
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:19,880
Chris has to work mostly
behind the scenes anyway.

53
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:26,600
Are you that happy?

54
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,000
Mm.

55
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:33,760
It feels like my abilities are
being acknowledged for the first time.

56
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,980
Then, I'll come up with more dishes.

57
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,100
There should be a lot of dishes
when you're promoting something new,

58
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:41,680
right?

59
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:44,360
I'll be back.

60
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:48,600
Did she really have to rush
to come up with new dishes?

61
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:51,960
[COME AGAIN, WE'RE CLOSED]

62
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:58,480
[Calling]

63
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:11,200
Who are you calling?

64
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,040
A friend...

65
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:15,640
Your friend who helped
you come up with the flower dishes?

66
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:18,120
Mm... yes.

67
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,440
That's nice.

68
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,720
I want to thank them as well

69
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,760
for making you want to
help me with my work.

70
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,000
And for making us...

71
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:33,240
closer...

72
00:05:41,320 --> 00:05:43,040
Don't do this, Nadear.

73
00:05:44,020 --> 00:05:45,040
That's right.

74
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,600
When we dated,

75
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:51,520
you wouldn't even let me kiss you.

76
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:54,680
Why would I expect anything now?

77
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:57,680
What are you expecting?

78
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:00,880
Change, perhaps?

79
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:05,840
I was willing to accept your flower dishes

80
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,840
in hopes that

81
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:12,540
you'd let me...

82
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:16,280
back into our relationship.

83
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:19,840
Back, you say?

84
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:32,320
I used to be in here, didn't I?

85
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:44,720
If my brain has an issue,

86
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:47,600
would my feelings change too, Doctor?

87
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:55,480
The brain...

88
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,440
controls your emotions, Chris.

89
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:02,920
My brain tells me I love Nadear,

90
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:06,160
but my feelings say otherwise.

91
00:07:08,140 --> 00:07:09,720
Who is right for you then?

92
00:07:14,960 --> 00:07:16,680
Can I tell you that?

93
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:18,800
It's a matter of medical ethics.

94
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:20,320
A patient's information is confidential.

95
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:26,760
But you don't seem like
that good of a person?

96
00:07:34,180 --> 00:07:35,560
That's true,

97
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:37,640
but I'm a good friend.

98
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:41,300
A friend's code.

99
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,460
I'll keep my friend's secret to myself.

100
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:48,360
I loved Nadear in the past.

101
00:07:51,260 --> 00:07:52,880
That means now...

102
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:59,440
If my memories returned,

103
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:01,880
would the Nadear I knew then

104
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:03,900
be the same person she is now?

105
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:09,240
Speaking as a doctor,

106
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:11,660
I'd say...

107
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:13,680
Our brains are complex.

108
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,360
And what if you answer as a friend?

109
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:19,840
Our hearts aren't as complex.

110
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:25,360
Chris is in love with someone else, isn't she?

111
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:29,800
I don't think so.

112
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:32,440
You're lying.

113
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:37,480
It might be that friend.

114
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:41,400
The one who taught her
to make those flower dishes.

115
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:43,040
And if it's true...

116
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:44,560
what will you do?

117
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:47,320
I should be asking you that.

118
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:50,520
What should I do?

119
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,240
You have to let her go.

120
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:56,000
You know I can't do that.

121
00:08:58,520 --> 00:08:59,880
What I mean is...

122
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,920
you need to give Chris more freedom.

123
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:05,200
Chris needs to be free

124
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:07,080
before she can choose who to love.

125
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:10,360
And what if she doesn't choose me?

126
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:19,160
Well, you have me.

127
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:29,000
Alright...

128
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:32,520
I'll give it a try.

129
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:40,600
You won't let Chris leave me, right?

130
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:57,400
This plant is hardy.

131
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:00,040
It's easy to take care of

132
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:02,140
and can purify the air as well.

133
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:07,960
Alright,

134
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:12,760
I'll help you out.

135
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:03,240
Oh, Chris?

136
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:04,200
Sun.

137
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,540
Is everything alright?

138
00:11:07,560 --> 00:11:08,840
Why are you here?

139
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:12,080
I couldn't contact you.

140
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:13,360
Are you alright?

141
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:15,240
I'm alright.

142
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:16,520
What about you?

143
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:18,240
You're not okay, are you?

144
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:22,760
I did it.

145
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:29,640
I told you you got this.

146
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:32,560
It's all thanks to you.

147
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:36,120
Does coming here have something
to do with me too?

148
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,920
I've always thought about you

149
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:42,120
ever since I made those dishes
for the customers.

150
00:11:46,660 --> 00:11:47,960
What were you thinking of me?

151
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:51,400
I think it's your compliments?

152
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:55,320
You always know what to say to cheer me up.

153
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:30,040
I kissed you,

154
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:33,100
because I don't want to be just friends.

155
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:40,280
What about you?

156
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:50,600
I don't love Nadear when I'm awake.

157
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:52,800
But every time I dream,

158
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,640
it's always about her.

159
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:58,140
The affection still lingers.

160
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:00,480
Your heart

161
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:02,640
might be more complex than your brain.

162
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,600
But be careful.

163
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:08,560
This won't only hurt you.

164
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:11,320
It'll hurt the others too.

165
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,080
So,

166
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:25,880
are we just friends?

167
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:30,080
Sun, you're a friend
I never want to hurt.

168
00:13:31,740 --> 00:13:33,280
Not even a little bit.

169
00:14:08,320 --> 00:14:09,520
Doctor Prung,

170
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:11,720
you came in without saying anything.

171
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:13,970
Well, when my sister does something,

172
00:14:13,990 --> 00:14:16,560
she doesn't seem to tell me either.

173
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:21,080
I didn't tell you,

174
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:22,240
but you knew anyway.

175
00:14:33,160 --> 00:14:34,960
This is even worse, Jeen.

176
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:44,200
It's not.

177
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:47,480
We still have hope.

178
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:49,200
What hope?

179
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:52,680
Chris...

180
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:54,680
will never love Nadear.

181
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:57,120
Never.

182
00:14:59,460 --> 00:15:01,040
That means...

183
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:02,570
Nadear

184
00:15:02,590 --> 00:15:03,880
will love you.

185
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,280
Do you really think that?

186
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:09,920
It means...

187
00:15:10,670 --> 00:15:11,880
this is the first time

188
00:15:13,820 --> 00:15:15,820
I'll do the right thing.

189
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,400
Aw...

190
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:30,680
That's good.

191
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:39,660
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

192
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:40,980
It seems like Chris

193
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:42,720
really enjoys working here.

194
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:47,880
Aren't you worried about
her being stressed anymore?

195
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,440
I'm going to a flower farm.
I'll be back in the evening.

196
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:05,200
With who?

197
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:07,320
A friend.

198
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:09,220
Her working here isn't as worrying as

199
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:11,200
going to the flower farm
with her friend again.

200
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:14,480
Wow.

201
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:17,200
It seems like Chris

202
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:19,480
has friends other than you.

203
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:22,200
Yes.

204
00:16:23,180 --> 00:16:24,300
It's a good thing

205
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:26,480
I have you, Nan.

206
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:30,320
You'll be by my side, right?

207
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,040
I have been with you all this time.

208
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:42,960
[Parking spot]

209
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:07,320
Is that your girlfriend?

210
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:08,560
Why don't you answer it?

211
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:13,640
[Nadear]

212
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:19,720
I'll go back soon.

213
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:21,520
I'll see you this evening.

214
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:28,400
You spoke so politely.

215
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:32,280
Not only is your girlfriend lucky,

216
00:17:33,440 --> 00:17:35,720
but you're lucky to have her too, huh?

217
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:41,820
I wanted it to be that way too.

218
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:44,360
What is your girlfriend like?

219
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:46,920
Well...

220
00:17:47,460 --> 00:17:49,560
She's a woman with long black hair,

221
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:52,000
and she smiles...

222
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,840
so much that I call her "Smiley."

223
00:17:57,740 --> 00:17:59,160
Smiley...?

224
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:02,400
Smiley.

225
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:12,800
[Third Person]

226
00:18:15,008 --> 00:18:17,808
[Third Person]

227
00:18:19,088 --> 00:18:20,668
The hotel

228
00:18:20,688 --> 00:18:24,048
picked up the edible flowers
a couple of hours ago.

229
00:18:24,308 --> 00:18:25,688
It was an urgent order.

230
00:18:25,948 --> 00:18:27,608
We truly apologize,

231
00:18:27,768 --> 00:18:29,848
but we do have other products
you can take a look at.

232
00:18:29,948 --> 00:18:30,968
It's alright.

233
00:18:30,988 --> 00:18:32,728
We came without an appointment.

234
00:18:34,988 --> 00:18:37,248
Not even a little bit left...?

235
00:18:42,848 --> 00:18:44,288
You have tulips here?

236
00:18:44,648 --> 00:18:45,588
Yes.

237
00:18:45,608 --> 00:18:47,748
Would you like to see them?
I'll tell the employees to guide you there.

238
00:18:47,768 --> 00:18:48,488
Yes, please.

239
00:18:48,848 --> 00:18:49,868
Thank you.

240
00:18:56,888 --> 00:18:57,848
Why are you smiling?

241
00:18:59,128 --> 00:19:00,248
Let's take some photos together.

242
00:19:02,568 --> 00:19:03,328
Let's go!

243
00:19:25,288 --> 00:19:26,328
Let's take a picture.

244
00:19:27,318 --> 00:19:27,848
Come on.

245
00:19:31,248 --> 00:19:31,968
Here.

246
00:19:58,988 --> 00:20:00,408
Chris, why are you looking at me like that?

247
00:20:00,848 --> 00:20:02,208
I'm just a bit surprised.

248
00:20:02,508 --> 00:20:04,208
I thought you only liked roses.

249
00:20:08,628 --> 00:20:11,128
If someone changes what they like,

250
00:20:12,648 --> 00:20:14,568
will their feelings stay the same?

251
00:20:17,728 --> 00:20:19,128
If I like tulips,

252
00:20:20,728 --> 00:20:21,968
not roses,

253
00:20:23,408 --> 00:20:25,408
will you still want to be friends with me?

254
00:20:29,888 --> 00:20:31,168
I like roses

255
00:20:32,388 --> 00:20:33,588
because I like you.

256
00:20:35,208 --> 00:20:37,368
But if you choose to like tulips,

257
00:20:39,488 --> 00:20:41,448
I'll like them too.

258
00:20:45,328 --> 00:20:46,248
Thank you.

259
00:20:48,448 --> 00:20:50,008
Keep your promise, alright?

260
00:21:07,768 --> 00:21:09,448
This feels familiar, huh?

261
00:21:12,408 --> 00:21:14,088
But today isn't the same.

262
00:21:14,948 --> 00:21:15,888
Why?

263
00:21:17,528 --> 00:21:19,048
Because we're just friends.

264
00:21:22,668 --> 00:21:23,408
Mm.

265
00:21:25,848 --> 00:21:27,288
Can you tell me why?

266
00:21:38,708 --> 00:21:40,328
The reason is...

267
00:21:41,088 --> 00:21:43,088
Don't be a bad person because of me, Sun.

268
00:22:01,088 --> 00:22:02,728
Do you have someone else?

269
00:22:13,488 --> 00:22:14,888
Why do you ask me that?

270
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:16,928
Why aren't you denying it?

271
00:22:18,728 --> 00:22:20,448
You do know

272
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:22,608
what our relationship is, don't you?

273
00:22:22,928 --> 00:22:24,688
But we're still dating.

274
00:22:26,568 --> 00:22:30,048
I won't let anyone come between us.

275
00:22:35,368 --> 00:22:36,488
If I do, I'll tell you.

276
00:22:37,868 --> 00:22:39,088
If you didn't,

277
00:22:41,768 --> 00:22:43,688
then why did you change?

278
00:22:46,748 --> 00:22:48,128
I can't even remember

279
00:22:48,948 --> 00:22:50,248
who I used to be,

280
00:22:51,488 --> 00:22:53,008
so how could I change?

281
00:22:53,848 --> 00:22:55,368
But I do...

282
00:22:57,788 --> 00:23:00,008
You used to care more about me.

283
00:23:01,288 --> 00:23:02,808
You heard me out.

284
00:23:03,648 --> 00:23:06,048
You listened to me.

285
00:23:06,448 --> 00:23:08,208
You trusted me.

286
00:23:09,608 --> 00:23:11,808
You never asked to break up with me.

287
00:23:13,788 --> 00:23:16,008
You used to make me smile.

288
00:23:21,808 --> 00:23:24,168
I want you to remember.

289
00:23:44,048 --> 00:23:44,928
Chris!

290
00:23:45,288 --> 00:23:46,328
Chris!

291
00:23:53,568 --> 00:23:54,488
Chris...

292
00:23:57,468 --> 00:23:59,728
I've always looked at you...

293
00:24:05,508 --> 00:24:08,048
I could feel your eyes

294
00:24:08,528 --> 00:24:10,648
always watching me.

295
00:24:11,168 --> 00:24:12,648
Is someone looking at me?

296
00:24:14,528 --> 00:24:15,368
Yeah.

297
00:24:15,568 --> 00:24:16,888
She didn't even look away.

298
00:24:17,648 --> 00:24:19,768
Ugh, what the heck is wrong with her?

299
00:24:20,688 --> 00:24:22,168
She's the new kid

300
00:24:22,408 --> 00:24:24,288
we asked to join our group yesterday.

301
00:24:24,528 --> 00:24:25,168
Huh?

302
00:24:25,708 --> 00:24:26,368
Mm.

303
00:24:26,848 --> 00:24:28,188
After talking to her...

304
00:24:28,208 --> 00:24:29,968
she seems pretty nice.

305
00:24:30,068 --> 00:24:33,028
She started school
a month after us because...

306
00:24:33,568 --> 00:24:35,488
she moved with her dad after he changed jobs.

307
00:24:47,108 --> 00:24:47,688
Ow.

308
00:24:49,608 --> 00:24:50,488
Chris!

309
00:25:00,448 --> 00:25:01,168
You!

310
00:25:01,308 --> 00:25:02,808
Run three laps around the field!

311
00:25:13,908 --> 00:25:15,968
Hey! Be more careful.

312
00:25:15,988 --> 00:25:18,368
Do you want to get caught
buying stuff from outside the school?

313
00:25:21,768 --> 00:25:22,968
Hey, you two!

314
00:25:23,028 --> 00:25:24,208
What are you doing?!

315
00:25:24,768 --> 00:25:25,368
Run!

316
00:25:27,128 --> 00:25:28,128
Get up there!

317
00:25:28,148 --> 00:25:28,988
Go!

318
00:25:31,368 --> 00:25:32,648
Get down, get down.

319
00:25:42,528 --> 00:25:44,288
Why did we have to run this far?

320
00:25:45,708 --> 00:25:47,208
Well, I was scared.

321
00:25:52,288 --> 00:25:53,208
Do you think...

322
00:25:54,728 --> 00:25:56,488
he'll find us here?

323
00:25:58,408 --> 00:25:59,348
Maybe he will

324
00:25:59,368 --> 00:26:01,608
if you keep letting the smell of meatballs
waft around like this.

325
00:26:07,868 --> 00:26:08,748
Did you know?

326
00:26:08,768 --> 00:26:10,768
This is my first time skipping class.

327
00:26:12,888 --> 00:26:15,508
If you weren't waiting for
your food out in the open like that,

328
00:26:15,528 --> 00:26:17,248
you wouldn't have
had your first time like this.

329
00:26:17,808 --> 00:26:19,408
We had to run for our lives, you see?

330
00:26:21,168 --> 00:26:22,368
It was fun, though.

331
00:26:23,608 --> 00:26:24,288
Huh?

332
00:26:26,128 --> 00:26:27,568
I said,

333
00:26:27,588 --> 00:26:29,888
skipping class with you today was fun.

334
00:26:32,368 --> 00:26:33,168
Want some?

335
00:26:43,168 --> 00:26:44,168
Smiley...

336
00:26:52,888 --> 00:26:54,008
It's me...

337
00:26:56,208 --> 00:26:58,368
Please be alright...

338
00:27:12,588 --> 00:27:14,768
You love the Nadear in your memories,

339
00:27:15,928 --> 00:27:17,808
but you want to break up with this Nadear?

340
00:27:21,048 --> 00:27:21,968
Why?

341
00:27:25,908 --> 00:27:27,448
Nadear used to smile a lot,

342
00:27:28,288 --> 00:27:29,648
until she loved me.

343
00:27:31,128 --> 00:27:32,208
That's a classic reason

344
00:27:32,808 --> 00:27:34,568
for breaking up.

345
00:27:35,408 --> 00:27:36,848
Is it really for her?

346
00:27:39,648 --> 00:27:42,288
Are you a psychiatrist or
an expert at hitting a sore spot?

347
00:27:43,408 --> 00:27:45,088
I told you, I'm your friend.

348
00:27:45,988 --> 00:27:47,988
I even meet you outside.

349
00:27:53,488 --> 00:27:56,008
If I could fall in love with
Nadear from the past,

350
00:27:57,408 --> 00:27:58,828
but not with

351
00:27:58,848 --> 00:28:00,248
the Nadear I know now,

352
00:28:01,248 --> 00:28:02,648
shouldn't that mean
I should break up with her?

353
00:28:02,788 --> 00:28:05,048
Does this have anything to do
with the new friend you just met?

354
00:28:08,808 --> 00:28:10,728
I never wanted to be just friends with her.

355
00:28:18,828 --> 00:28:22,028
[Third Person]

356
00:28:24,331 --> 00:28:27,031
[Third Person]

357
00:28:39,631 --> 00:28:40,951
You again?

358
00:28:43,091 --> 00:28:44,391
Shouldn't I be asking you that?

359
00:28:45,231 --> 00:28:47,871
You know full well the reason

360
00:28:48,011 --> 00:28:48,951
people come here.

361
00:28:50,451 --> 00:28:51,951
I can't contact Sun.

362
00:28:54,551 --> 00:28:56,751
I know what Sun thinks of you,

363
00:28:57,231 --> 00:29:00,271
but she can't move on from you
because you act like this.

364
00:29:01,251 --> 00:29:03,671
She already has a lot of
problems in her life.

365
00:29:04,591 --> 00:29:06,791
Can't you keep your distance from her?

366
00:29:09,071 --> 00:29:10,471
Is there something going on?

367
00:29:18,831 --> 00:29:19,871
Hello, Sun,

368
00:29:20,051 --> 00:29:21,031
where are you?

369
00:29:21,471 --> 00:29:22,671
Can we meet?

370
00:29:24,071 --> 00:29:25,791
I want to talk about something.

371
00:29:28,811 --> 00:29:29,431
Huh?

372
00:29:30,951 --> 00:29:32,351
Then can I go with you?

373
00:29:38,251 --> 00:29:39,751
Excuse me, I'd like to change my destination.

374
00:29:41,031 --> 00:29:42,031
Okay.

375
00:29:45,071 --> 00:29:48,591
[VERITY SKIN CLINIC]

376
00:30:02,751 --> 00:30:03,511
How are you doing?

377
00:30:07,691 --> 00:30:08,951
Is this cocoa?

378
00:30:19,671 --> 00:30:20,751
I feel better now.

379
00:30:21,591 --> 00:30:22,831
You're so stressed, aren't you?

380
00:30:25,031 --> 00:30:25,871
Mm...

381
00:30:27,061 --> 00:30:28,791
Looking at the expenses...

382
00:30:29,451 --> 00:30:31,071
it's quite troubling to me.

383
00:30:35,271 --> 00:30:36,791
I was in an accident,

384
00:30:38,311 --> 00:30:40,831
so my father sent me abroad for treatment.

385
00:30:41,771 --> 00:30:42,951
Now that I've recovered,

386
00:30:45,911 --> 00:30:48,391
I want to repay my debts to my father.

387
00:30:50,871 --> 00:30:52,031
But look at this...

388
00:31:00,051 --> 00:31:01,311
An accident?

389
00:31:02,751 --> 00:31:03,591
When did it happen?

390
00:31:07,311 --> 00:31:08,951
Four years ago...

391
00:31:12,531 --> 00:31:13,751
That was around the same time as mine.

392
00:31:14,631 --> 00:31:15,431
Yeah.

393
00:31:18,271 --> 00:31:20,151
There is so much to think about,

394
00:31:21,351 --> 00:31:23,271
so everything seems necessary.

395
00:31:27,351 --> 00:31:29,351
Actually, I have some savings...

396
00:31:30,911 --> 00:31:32,111
Don't, Chris.

397
00:31:37,811 --> 00:31:39,631
You've just said that we should be friends.

398
00:31:41,551 --> 00:31:43,551
We've just known each other.

399
00:31:45,091 --> 00:31:46,431
Don't do this...

400
00:31:49,351 --> 00:31:50,371
How about this?

401
00:31:53,071 --> 00:31:54,751
Let's do what you've told me before.

402
00:31:58,251 --> 00:32:00,391
Choose what fits you perfectly

403
00:32:00,991 --> 00:32:02,031
so you feel at ease

404
00:32:02,711 --> 00:32:03,791
and not uncomfortable.

405
00:32:08,591 --> 00:32:09,651
Then...

406
00:32:13,711 --> 00:32:15,311
Can you stay here with me?

407
00:32:17,211 --> 00:32:19,071
When I'm with you...

408
00:32:21,811 --> 00:32:23,311
I feel exactly like that.

409
00:32:28,351 --> 00:32:29,811
[VERITY SKIN CLINIC]
["Reveal The True You"]

410
00:32:29,831 --> 00:32:32,151
Is there anything else
you'd like to put in this room?

411
00:32:33,111 --> 00:32:34,691
I think so.

412
00:32:34,711 --> 00:32:36,091
Let me think about it.

413
00:32:36,111 --> 00:32:37,471
Don't go over budget, okay?

414
00:32:41,391 --> 00:32:44,231
I think this equipment
can only be placed here.

415
00:32:46,551 --> 00:32:48,511
But we already went way over budget.

416
00:32:48,751 --> 00:32:50,751
If we buy this equipment,

417
00:32:50,891 --> 00:32:52,711
we won't have enough money
for the more important one.

418
00:32:53,471 --> 00:32:55,411
If we put both pieces of equipment there,

419
00:32:55,431 --> 00:32:57,331
it...it really won't work out.

420
00:32:57,351 --> 00:32:59,111
Is there anywhere else we can cut back?

421
00:32:59,471 --> 00:33:00,971
I agree with you, Doctor Sun.

422
00:33:00,991 --> 00:33:02,351
This is perfect.

423
00:33:02,491 --> 00:33:03,791
It's not very risky either.

424
00:33:05,711 --> 00:33:07,691
I didn't come up with it.

425
00:33:07,711 --> 00:33:08,791
Chris helped me.

426
00:33:08,851 --> 00:33:09,871
Wow...

427
00:33:11,271 --> 00:33:13,991
Iced lemon tea can
help in hot weather like this.

428
00:33:14,011 --> 00:33:14,811
- This is yours, Doctor.
- Thank you.

429
00:33:14,831 --> 00:33:15,571
Thank you.

430
00:33:15,591 --> 00:33:16,231
Here.

431
00:33:16,791 --> 00:33:17,431
Here.

432
00:33:18,231 --> 00:33:19,351
This is yours.

433
00:33:19,711 --> 00:33:20,411
Thanks.

434
00:33:20,431 --> 00:33:21,191
Are you tired?

435
00:33:21,411 --> 00:33:22,311
A little bit.

436
00:33:26,091 --> 00:33:27,151
I'm impressed.

437
00:33:27,471 --> 00:33:29,071
Ms. Chris, you're quite talented.

438
00:33:34,971 --> 00:33:37,031
She's very detail-oriented

439
00:33:40,071 --> 00:33:41,791
and caring.

440
00:33:49,311 --> 00:33:50,191
That's nice.

441
00:33:50,431 --> 00:33:53,431
Then...can we ask you
to be our consultant?

442
00:33:57,151 --> 00:33:58,191
Of course.

443
00:33:58,631 --> 00:33:59,631
Thank you so much.

444
00:34:02,291 --> 00:34:03,351
Here, I'll hold it for you.

445
00:34:04,791 --> 00:34:06,471
Overall, this looks okay now.

446
00:34:07,831 --> 00:34:09,671
I like being useful.

447
00:34:10,911 --> 00:34:12,191
But right now...

448
00:34:12,511 --> 00:34:14,671
I'm more curious about

449
00:34:15,431 --> 00:34:17,991
how Sun acts like she knows me well.

450
00:34:24,531 --> 00:34:27,031
Are you thanking me
by buying me something you like to eat?

451
00:34:28,191 --> 00:34:29,731
Give it a taste.

452
00:34:29,751 --> 00:34:31,471
You might like it, Chris.

453
00:34:39,431 --> 00:34:40,351
Yes,

454
00:34:40,711 --> 00:34:41,911
I do like it...

455
00:34:43,231 --> 00:34:44,591
How did she know that?

456
00:34:45,111 --> 00:34:46,731
Your face is very telling.

457
00:34:52,791 --> 00:34:53,791
You finally smiled.

458
00:34:54,651 --> 00:34:55,231
Hm?

459
00:34:56,631 --> 00:34:58,871
Well, you hardly smiled today.

460
00:35:00,431 --> 00:35:03,071
My life isn't exactly
full of things to smile about.

461
00:35:04,351 --> 00:35:05,111
So...

462
00:35:05,491 --> 00:35:07,071
You came to see me.
Is something going on?

463
00:35:10,071 --> 00:35:11,791
I came to see your smile.

464
00:35:12,631 --> 00:35:13,271
Hm?

465
00:35:17,511 --> 00:35:18,311
So...

466
00:35:19,071 --> 00:35:20,191
Seen enough?

467
00:35:35,391 --> 00:35:38,591
Didn't you say that Chris remembered
dating me in high school?

468
00:35:41,111 --> 00:35:42,511
Hello, Prung.

469
00:35:42,751 --> 00:35:44,471
I'm sorry, I didn't see you there.

470
00:35:47,791 --> 00:35:48,951
It's okay, Dear.

471
00:35:49,511 --> 00:35:51,911
Prung...already knew everything.

472
00:35:55,111 --> 00:35:56,711
Chris remembers that.

473
00:35:57,071 --> 00:35:58,471
I already talked to her.

474
00:36:00,991 --> 00:36:02,831
Then why isn't she
falling for me yet?

475
00:36:03,851 --> 00:36:05,151
She's a doctor,

476
00:36:05,431 --> 00:36:06,831
not a shaman.

477
00:36:07,271 --> 00:36:08,711
She can't make love potions.

478
00:36:09,691 --> 00:36:10,311
Prung.

479
00:36:14,751 --> 00:36:17,071
It's because you only focus on the past.

480
00:36:17,311 --> 00:36:19,591
The "past" that can't be changed,

481
00:36:20,031 --> 00:36:21,711
instead of the present.

482
00:36:22,631 --> 00:36:24,271
It's not just about her amnesia,

483
00:36:24,831 --> 00:36:26,671
but also about a relationship between lovers.

484
00:36:27,111 --> 00:36:28,991
A relationship should be about the present.

485
00:36:35,631 --> 00:36:37,071
You wouldn't understand

486
00:36:37,991 --> 00:36:39,031
how important the "past"

487
00:36:39,311 --> 00:36:41,431
is to me.

488
00:36:51,551 --> 00:36:52,951
Are you sure you don't want me
to drive you home?

489
00:36:53,211 --> 00:36:55,371
You already have a lot to
think about. Rest up.

490
00:36:59,491 --> 00:37:00,351
Thanks.

491
00:37:04,911 --> 00:37:05,471
Sun,

492
00:37:12,731 --> 00:37:14,511
something sweet to help relieve stress.

493
00:37:25,391 --> 00:37:26,551
I'll go now.

494
00:37:28,151 --> 00:37:28,871
Mm.

495
00:37:31,151 --> 00:37:35,091
♫Your smile is always so bright♫

496
00:37:35,111 --> 00:37:39,031
♫The smile imprinted in my heart♫

497
00:37:40,471 --> 00:37:46,051
♫Shining like the Sun♫

498
00:37:46,071 --> 00:37:48,370
♫Providing warm embrace,♫

499
00:37:48,395 --> 00:37:51,717
♫Always being near, hugging you tight,♫

500
00:37:51,742 --> 00:37:55,831
♫So you don't shed a tear♫

501
00:37:56,351 --> 00:38:01,871
♫If you had to face the storm,♫

502
00:38:03,831 --> 00:38:04,991
Thank you...

503
00:38:06,351 --> 00:38:10,231
♫The Sun will be there, shining in the sky♫

504
00:38:11,791 --> 00:38:14,871
Thank you for not making me
regret coming back here.

505
00:38:20,271 --> 00:38:23,311
[Third Person]

506
00:38:25,611 --> 00:38:28,311
[Third Person]

507
00:39:12,591 --> 00:39:15,071
[Happy Anniversary]

508
00:39:25,451 --> 00:39:27,391
The accident that happened four years ago

509
00:39:27,991 --> 00:39:30,071
almost took you away from me.

510
00:39:33,471 --> 00:39:35,211
I called your name every day

511
00:39:36,931 --> 00:39:38,351
until you regained consciousness.

512
00:39:39,991 --> 00:39:43,351
But you kept staring out
the window with tears in your eyes,

513
00:39:44,151 --> 00:39:46,471
and refused to talk for five months.

514
00:39:47,951 --> 00:39:50,311
You had severe depression.

515
00:39:50,971 --> 00:39:52,511
Your body was wounded.

516
00:39:52,831 --> 00:39:54,831
You were traumatized.

517
00:39:55,491 --> 00:39:57,871
Your brain shut out the pain,

518
00:39:58,731 --> 00:40:00,431
blocking out everything else.

519
00:40:08,471 --> 00:40:09,431
Jeen.

520
00:40:15,151 --> 00:40:17,071
Then you started to remember.

521
00:40:19,911 --> 00:40:20,591
Here.

522
00:40:22,171 --> 00:40:23,511
Did you buy these to give to people?

523
00:40:24,671 --> 00:40:25,551
No,

524
00:40:25,711 --> 00:40:26,951
they're offerings for Buddha.

525
00:40:27,951 --> 00:40:29,711
Then no thanks. I don't want to
take one meant for Buddha.

526
00:40:30,391 --> 00:40:32,071
This one isn't an offering.

527
00:40:32,811 --> 00:40:34,471
I want to give it to you.

528
00:41:03,811 --> 00:41:06,871
You lost your parents in that accident,

529
00:41:09,371 --> 00:41:10,491
while I...

530
00:41:13,351 --> 00:41:14,991
I lost you.

531
00:41:19,131 --> 00:41:20,511
I only thought

532
00:41:20,871 --> 00:41:24,391
I wanted you to remember
how we used to love each other.

533
00:41:26,151 --> 00:41:28,391
I wanted our relationship to go back
to how it used to be,

534
00:41:30,591 --> 00:41:34,391
and that made me completely ignore
what we have now.

535
00:41:37,371 --> 00:41:38,591
I'm sorry.

536
00:41:43,071 --> 00:41:43,911
Nadear...

537
00:41:44,711 --> 00:41:45,631
Chris...

538
00:41:53,351 --> 00:41:56,111
I asked you not to break up with me,

539
00:41:58,591 --> 00:42:00,391
not because of my parents,

540
00:42:05,191 --> 00:42:07,071
but because I love you.

541
00:42:12,711 --> 00:42:14,871
Can you give me another chance?

542
00:42:23,871 --> 00:42:24,831
I can't, Nadear.

543
00:42:25,891 --> 00:42:27,111
I can't love you.

544
00:42:28,571 --> 00:42:29,791
Chris, why?

545
00:42:30,491 --> 00:42:32,151
You only have me.

546
00:42:34,571 --> 00:42:36,751
The one who laughs while looking at you.

547
00:42:39,471 --> 00:42:41,551
The one who skipped class with you.

548
00:42:42,471 --> 00:42:44,591
The one who bought you roses.

549
00:42:45,571 --> 00:42:47,671
It's all me, Chris.

550
00:42:50,591 --> 00:42:51,871
That's not it.

551
00:42:54,291 --> 00:42:55,751
That's not it, Nadear.

552
00:42:56,351 --> 00:42:57,431
Chris...

553
00:42:59,691 --> 00:43:01,711
I can't, I can't, I can't...

554
00:43:01,731 --> 00:43:04,371
Nadear, this isn't right. I can't, it's...

555
00:43:05,571 --> 00:43:06,431
Chris!

556
00:43:07,551 --> 00:43:11,031
I don't know why I'm like this.

557
00:43:13,731 --> 00:43:17,111
I don't want to keep living like
this anymore, Nadear.

558
00:43:17,291 --> 00:43:18,191
Chris...

559
00:43:31,331 --> 00:43:32,231
Alright,

560
00:43:37,191 --> 00:43:38,351
I give up.

561
00:43:42,971 --> 00:43:45,471
Can you give me three months?

562
00:43:50,591 --> 00:43:53,551
Three months to go back
to how it used to be.

563
00:43:58,471 --> 00:44:01,271
Then I won't ask anything from you again.

564
00:44:13,951 --> 00:44:15,351
Chris, please?

565
00:44:51,331 --> 00:44:53,711
[Happy Anniversary]

566
00:44:59,231 --> 00:45:00,551
What do you mean, "three months"?

567
00:45:01,261 --> 00:45:02,911
You broke up a long time ago,

568
00:45:03,771 --> 00:45:06,591
but you plan to date her again
for three months?

569
00:45:07,851 --> 00:45:09,951
It's my final gambit.

570
00:45:11,611 --> 00:45:12,711
What are you going to do?

571
00:45:16,951 --> 00:45:18,551
I'll make Chris

572
00:45:20,991 --> 00:45:22,291
mine...

573
00:45:25,271 --> 00:45:26,871
by any means necessary.

574
00:45:32,731 --> 00:45:34,271
So you acted weird

575
00:45:35,711 --> 00:45:37,311
because you want to be friends with me

576
00:45:38,491 --> 00:45:40,491
so that you can cut ties with your ex.

577
00:45:42,791 --> 00:45:43,591
Mm...

578
00:45:44,471 --> 00:45:45,911
But I couldn't do it.

579
00:45:47,531 --> 00:45:49,811
And I even gave her three months.

580
00:45:51,731 --> 00:45:53,031
You gave in because

581
00:45:53,671 --> 00:45:54,951
you still love her, don't you?

582
00:46:02,711 --> 00:46:04,991
She used to be someone important to me.

583
00:46:07,751 --> 00:46:09,471
This sounds like we're having an affair.

584
00:46:12,091 --> 00:46:14,631
I really don't want you to be
a bad person because of me.

585
00:46:16,831 --> 00:46:19,511
We were wrong from
that very first kiss, Chris.

586
00:46:22,191 --> 00:46:23,711
Will God punish us?

587
00:46:25,451 --> 00:46:26,831
This pain

588
00:46:27,671 --> 00:46:29,331
is God's punishment.

589
00:46:31,171 --> 00:46:33,511
Can I still make things right?

590
00:46:35,491 --> 00:46:36,191
Mm.

591
00:46:37,271 --> 00:46:38,191
I'll wait.

592
00:46:40,751 --> 00:46:41,911
Wait for what?

593
00:46:43,551 --> 00:46:46,551
Three months might be long enough
for you to love someone else.

594
00:46:48,131 --> 00:46:51,231
Or it might be long enough
for you to decide we should be just friends.

595
00:47:04,511 --> 00:47:05,871
But three months

596
00:47:05,931 --> 00:47:08,311
is long enough for you

597
00:47:09,051 --> 00:47:11,051
to tell love from indebtedness.

598
00:47:24,271 --> 00:47:25,591
I know what love is

599
00:47:27,771 --> 00:47:29,311
ever since I first met you.

600
00:47:35,831 --> 00:47:45,571
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

601
00:47:45,591 --> 00:47:50,691
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

602
00:47:50,711 --> 00:47:54,591
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

603
00:47:54,811 --> 00:48:00,811
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

604
00:48:00,831 --> 00:48:10,551
♫The storm grows heavier, demanding an answer♫

605
00:48:11,231 --> 00:48:12,591
I'll make things right

606
00:48:13,711 --> 00:48:15,051
after three months.

607
00:48:15,251 --> 00:48:16,511
Don't you think

608
00:48:16,991 --> 00:48:18,951
she can keep asking for more time?

609
00:48:19,431 --> 00:48:21,431
But it's important to me too.

610
00:48:21,791 --> 00:48:23,391
It's really you, huh?

611
00:48:23,821 --> 00:48:25,821
How was she doing

612
00:48:26,511 --> 00:48:27,911
after that accident four years ago?

613
00:48:28,091 --> 00:48:29,631
Sun lost her memories back then.

614
00:48:30,031 --> 00:48:31,591
I think Sun got her memories back.

615
00:48:33,311 --> 00:48:34,311
Sun...

616
00:48:34,911 --> 00:48:35,911
is my friend...?

617
00:48:49,751 --> 00:48:59,631
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

618
